Ubuntu adaptation (2026): native Python/Tk desktop interface, Linux process
and PE-module discovery, build validation, guarded data-only memory backend,
rate-limited diagnostics, tests, and packaging. Oxygen, health, fall-speed,
and jump behaviour and offsets are adapted from upstream client/features/
and client/games/trr-123/. The original pinned upstream source is included.

This application is an independent adaptation, not an upstream release.
No proprietary game files, saves, or extracted Windows application are included.
The optional Frida research runtime uses its own licence; it is not part of the
runtime package. The application itself needs only Python 3 and Tk.

Original logo.png, burn.png, burn_256.png and burn.ico are preserved byte-for-byte
from upstream client/ui/images. The header, stop, folder and related icon SVG
geometry is imported from client/ui/launcher.html; PNG renderings adapt it for Tk.
The Windows branding is reused with attribution; this is an independent Linux port.
